== answer ==
Replaced ``# One CI gate, one file (issue #991).
#
# PR #1188: R1188-U6 and R1188-U7, the links notation we own is measured.
ci_gate check-notation
  stage web
  description "R1188-U6/U7: the links notation we own (the scopes of data/meta/notation-rules.lino) holds at most the ceilings of data/meta/notation-ratchet.lino of distinct names spelled with `_`, names holding a seeded abbreviation, duplicated child blocks and repeated fields; the ceilings only fall. The rename rule's --check fails when a notation file or a reader literal holds a name the rule renamed (data/meta/notation-renames.lino) in its old spelling."
  run "node scripts/measure-notation.mjs --check && node experiments/formal_ai_subagent/apply-notation-rules.mjs --check"
  justification "PR #1188 (R1188-U6, R1188-U7, owner 2026-10-08): names prefer `-` over `_`, use full English words, and shared structure is stated once. The rule passes lower these counts family by family; without a gate a new `_` name or a repeated block would raise them again unnoticed. The measure takes under a second."
`` with `# PR #1188: CI documentation, response templates and Pages trust

- Repair Rust documentation, formatting, ordered module declarations and Clippy diagnostics reported by the first CI compile of the current changes.
- Carry renamed handler captures through localized response placeholders and browser bootstrap templates. Repository traffic answers now render both official documentation links in all five languages, for named and unnamed repositories. Preserve Rust formatting variables and unrelated template fields.
- Build Pages only from the trusted triggering ref, accept a full commit SHA, and verify that the checkout matches the selected release commit before executing repository code. Fail explicitly if the release branch moved.

Validation: 17 nearest planner regression tests and 13 notation/Pages tests pass; standalone Rust formatting and the notation gate pass. All source edits were executed by Formal AI, or by the existing notation and TypeScript generators. Rust compilation and CodeQL verification run in CI.
` in `changelog.d/20261009_031500_ci-templates-and-pages-trust.md` and observed the result.
